Upload
typescriptnew PutObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key, Body, ContentType })
Download
typescriptnew GetObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key })
Delete single
typescriptnew DeleteObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key })
Delete multiple
typescriptnew DeleteObjectsCommand({
  Bucket,
  Delete: {
    Objects: [{ Key: 'file1.png' }, { Key: 'file2.png' }]
  }
})
List objects
typescriptnew ListObjectsV2Command({ Bucket, Prefix: 'folder/' })
Presigned URL (get)
typescriptimport { getSignedUrl } from '@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner'

const url = await getSignedUrl(client, new GetObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key }), { expiresIn: 3600 })
Presigned URL (upload)
typescriptconst url = await getSignedUrl(client, new PutObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key }), { expiresIn: 3600 })
Check if object exists
typescriptnew HeadObjectCommand({ Bucket, Key })
Copy object
typescriptnew CopyObjectCommand({ Bucket, CopySource: 'bucket/oldkey', Key: 'newkey' })
All work the same way — await client.send(new XCommand({...})). Same for R2 since it's S3 compatible.